<Legal title="Terms of use" updated="2026-11-06">
  <h2>What ImageFactory is</h2>
  <p>
    ImageFactory makes images for you when you ask an AI assistant such as Claude or ChatGPT, or call our API. It is
    offered as a private service and an account may be limited or closed at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Your content</h2>
  <p>
    You keep the rights you have in your prompts, brand kits and reference images, and you confirm you may upload and
    use them. The images are generated by an AI model. Results can contain mistakes, including misspelled text, and they
    may resemble existing works. Check an image before you publish or print it.
  </p>

  <h2>Public image links</h2>
  <p>
    Every generated image is served from a public web address that anyone who has the link can open. The address is
    long and random, but it is not private. Do not generate images you need to keep confidential. Deleting an image
    stops its link from working. Brand reference images are private and are never served from a public address.
  </p>

  <h2>Credits</h2>
  <p>
    Images are paid for with credits. Credits are reserved when you ask for an image and charged only for images that are
    delivered. Credits have no cash value and are not refundable unless the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Do not use ImageFactory to make unlawful content, content that targets or sexualises minors, deceptive material about
    real people, or anything that infringes someone else's rights. Do not try to bypass the safety checks, share your
    keys, or put load on the service that affects other people.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability and liability</h2>
  <p>
    The service is provided as is. It depends on third parties and may be unavailable or change. To the extent the law
    allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, and our total liability is limited to the credits you
    bought in the previous three months.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
